From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 18:36:07 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] clk: sunxi-ng: Add the A733 SERDES CCU

The SERDES block of the A733 has a small clock and reset unit at its
start, with the AHB and AXI bus gates of the USB3 controller, the
select of its PIPE clock and the reset of the USB 2.0 PHY of that
controller.

Add a driver for it. Its registers read as zero and ignore writes while
the SERDES reset is asserted, and the board hangs once the SERDES bus
matrix gates in front of it are closed as unused. The driver therefore
deasserts the reset, shared with the SERDES PHYs, and keeps the matrix
gates enabled while it is bound.

The PIPE clock select (SUBSYS_USB3P1_BGR bit 20, user manual 18.2.6.2)
takes the PIPE clock of the controller from the CCU instead of the combo
PHY. The CCU clock is usb2-u2-pipe, which the manual lists as a clock
source of the USB3.1 controller (18.4.3). The PIPE clock of the PHY is
no clock of the tree, so the select is a gate on usb2-u2-pipe and not a
mux: while it is enabled, the controller runs on the CCU's PIPE clock. A
PHY driver that takes the SuperSpeed lanes away from the controller
enables it.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: booted on two boards with the driver built
in; the board stays up after the unused clocks are closed, the USB3
controller binds with the PIPE clock select held by the combo PHY, the
PCIe link to an NVMe drive comes up, and the USB3 and PCIe gate and
reset registers of the block read back as the driver sets them.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/Kconfig                  |  11 ++
 drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/Makefile                 |   2 +
 drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/ccu-sun60i-a733-serdes.c | 142 ++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 155 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/ccu-sun60i-a733-serdes.c

diff --git a/drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/Kconfig b/drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/Kconfig
index cffa83056934..978c1459c599 100644
--- a/drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/Kconfig
@@ -77,6 +77,17 @@ config SUN60I_A733_R_CCU
 	default ARCH_SUNXI
 	depends on ARM64 || COMPILE_TEST
 
+config SUN60I_A733_SERDES_CCU
+	tristate "Support for the Allwinner A733 SERDES CCU"
+	default ARCH_SUNXI
+	depends on ARM64 || COMPILE_TEST
+	help
+	  Support for the clock and reset unit of the SERDES block on the
+	  Allwinner A733. It provides the bus clocks of the USB3 controller,
+	  the select of its PIPE clock and the reset of its USB 2.0 PHY,
+	  and keeps the SERDES bus matrix gates of the main clock unit
+	  running while it is bound.
+
 config SUN4I_A10_CCU
 	tristate "Support for the Allwinner A10/A20 CCU"
 	default ARCH_SUNXI
diff --git a/drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/Makefile b/drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/Makefile
index 3a39eb9287da..7cab2eac35a9 100644
--- a/drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/Makefile
+++ b/drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/Makefile
@@ -38,6 +38,7 @@ obj-$(CONFIG_SUN55I_A523_MCU_CCU)	+= sun55i-a523-mcu-ccu.o
 obj-$(CONFIG_SUN55I_A523_R_CCU)	+= sun55i-a523-r-ccu.o
 obj-$(CONFIG_SUN60I_A733_CCU)	+= sun60i-a733-ccu.o
 obj-$(CONFIG_SUN60I_A733_R_CCU)	+= sun60i-a733-r-ccu.o
+obj-$(CONFIG_SUN60I_A733_SERDES_CCU)	+= sun60i-a733-serdes-ccu.o
 obj-$(CONFIG_SUN4I_A10_CCU)	+= sun4i-a10-ccu.o
 obj-$(CONFIG_SUN5I_CCU)		+= sun5i-ccu.o
